1
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,910
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

2
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:22,910
(No, It Can't!!)

3
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:34,990
Love's Chocolate Cosmos

4
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,700
'Sup, Natsume! Morning.

5
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,320
M-Morning.

6
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,230
Nice, is this new?

7
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,610
I borrowed it from my sister.

8
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,250
That's cool.

9
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:42,050
<i>One minor new development...</i>

10
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:42,450
Figures why it's girly.

11
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,410
Is it weird?

12
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:46,560
<i>I made a friend besides Himari.</i>

13
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:46,540
Nah, you pull it off.

14
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,240
By the way, where's Himari-chan?

15
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:49,660
I haven't seen her yet—

16
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,220
Ha! Gotcha!

17
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:52,460
H-Himari?

18
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:54,560
Hey, Himari-chan. Morning!

19
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,530
Morning!

20
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:58,280
You two besties seem to be getting along.

21
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,330
<i>"Look at you, getting friendly 
with the side bestie."</i>

22
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,790
<i>"I thought I was number one, 
but I see how it is."</i>

23
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:04,860
<i>Is that it?</i>

24
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:07,320
Hey, nice coat.

25
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,460
Where'd you get it?

26
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,110
It's his sister's.

27
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:12,440
Oh, no wonder it's so cute.

28
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,940
<i>Before I knew it, we were a group of three.</i>

29
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,520
Yu!

30
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,780
It's almost time for the Christmas exhibit!

31
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,500
Have you decided on the flowers?

32
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,790
F-For the most part.

33
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:29,880
<i>My life's been fun 
ever since meeting Himari.</i>

34
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:34,090
<i>As long as she likes my work, it's worth it.</i>

35
00:02:34,950 --> 00:02:36,590
Hey, about Christmas...

36
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,300
Himari-chan mentioned 
having plans that day, right?

37
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,790
What? Really?

38
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:44,520
She said she was coming to the exhibit.

39
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:49,440
Natsume, I've got a huge favor to ask.

40
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:53,420
Could I have some time alone 
with Himari-chan on Christmas?

41
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,270
<i>It's not like she needs 
to be at the exhibit.</i>

42
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:04,030
<i>Besides, I don't want Himari 
hating romance forever.</i>

43
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:08,000
<i>So I lied and said that the
 exhibit was canceled.</i>

44
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,620
<i>I hope it works out between them.</i>

45
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:13,240
Natsume-kun, let's grab some lunch.

46
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:15,210
Ramen 
Kadoya

47
00:03:14,370 --> 00:03:15,220
Sensei.

48
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:21,360
Say you had a friend that 
was better off with someone else.

49
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,340
I think true friendship 
is about letting them

50
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:28,240
spend time with that 
other person over yourself.

51
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,640
What do you think?

52
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,950
Hmm...

53
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:34,220
It's like with flowers.

54
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:39,000
Sometimes, flowers grow better 
when you plant two or three seeds together.

55
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,070
Instead of just one by itself.

56
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,690
<i>Wait, is that even true?</i>

57
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:50,040
Hey, you!

58
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,000
No slacking at the reception desk.

59
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:55,400
Wh-What are you doing here?

60
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,020
I visited your place 
and they said you were here.

61
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:00,640
Yeah... well...

62
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,200
Why didn't you hang out with him?

63
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:07,230
I did. Not for long, though.

64
00:04:07,230 --> 00:04:09,220
I only went because he said you'd be there.

65
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:14,070
By the way, what was that all about?

66
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:17,590
He was all serious 
and confessed his love to me.

67
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:19,600
So gross. That kind of tactic is the worst.

68
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,800
B-But he's a good guy.

69
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,950
I was just hoping you two 
would be happy together.

70
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,080
Yu, are you serious?

71
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:30,760
That guy used you to get closer to me.

72
00:04:31,490 --> 00:04:33,020
He's been trying to get with me

73
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:35,040
before you and I started hanging out.

74
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:42,160
I kept quiet hoping he genuinely 
wanted to be friends with you.

75
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:49,230
So no more cheating on me, okay?

76
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,560
Who's cheating?

77
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,840
Is this one yours?

78
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,660
How did you know?

79
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,790
Don't tell me, was I your main inspo?

80
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,750
Wh-Why do you ask?

81
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,470
The meaning of my name.

82
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:12,920
"Himari" means "sunflower."

83
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,090
Th-That's just a coincidence.

84
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,180
<i>I lied.</i>

85
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:22,330
<i>I made that piece for Himari.</i>

86
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,760
<i>The sunflowers mean...</i>

87
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,600
<i>"I only see you."</i>

88
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:30,010
<i>Like Himari's friendship.</i>

89
00:05:30,010 --> 00:05:31,680
<i>Straight as an arrow.</i>

90
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,090
Hey, Yu.

91
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:39,860
If you care about me, 
don't go trying to set me up.

92
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:40,540
Huh?

93
00:05:40,930 --> 00:05:45,120
If I end up with someone else, 
that would leave you all alone.

94
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,150
That's not good.

95
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,280
You and I are best friends.

96
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:52,720
But there's no way we'd each 
find someone at the same time.

97
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,120
Probably!

98
00:05:54,410 --> 00:05:57,480
But we should fix 
that bad habit of yours first.

99
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,450
I guess I'll do my best.

100
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,390
Promise you'll only see me forever?

101
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,390
I'm your only best friend after all.

102
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,910
Bwa-ha!

103
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:19,920
So?

104
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,070
What do you think about this wreath?

105
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,060
Hmm... Five out of ten!

106
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:28,860
It's good, but it feels incomplete.

107
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:31,470
I wish you'd get to know me better first.

108
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,790
One day, when you feel complete...

109
00:06:37,170 --> 00:06:38,850
Promise to show me first!

110
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,130
<i>Ever since I was little,</i>

111
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:48,240
<i>I was always bad at making stuff.</i>

112
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:50,610
<i>Hey, look at that cutie.</i>

113
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:55,490
<i>Whatever. The world's full of 
good-looking people.</i>

114
00:06:56,580 --> 00:07:01,250
<i>Even a pretty girl like me 
has worries on her mind.</i>

115
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,680
This one needs water, too.

116
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,320
<i>Chocolate cosmos.</i>

117
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:08,840
<i>Obviously, they smell like chocolate.</i>

118
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,780
<i>They bloom in the fall.</i>

119
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,490
Yu!

120
00:07:12,490 --> 00:07:13,790
Good morning!

121
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,010
Morning!

122
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:23,470
<i>He's texting Enocchi.</i>

123
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,570
Hey, Yu?

124
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:29,110
'S-Sup, Himari. Morning.

125
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:32,510
Hey, it's dangerous to text while you walk.

126
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:33,440
R-Right...

127
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,430
<i>Look up already!</i>

128
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:38,670
<i>It's like he's glued to the screen.</i>

129
00:07:38,670 --> 00:07:40,230
<i>I'm not giving up, though!</i>

130
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:43,240
Have any plans for summer break?

131
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,740
Oh yeah, it starts soon.

132
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:46,960
Accessories are great and all,

133
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,700
but next year will be all 
about entrance exams.

134
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,930
This may be our last summer to have fun!

135
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,570
Wanna spend the night, just the two of us?

136
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:57,360
A-A-Are you stupid?

137
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,550
We can't do that!

138
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:01,130
Why not? We're best friends!

139
00:08:01,130 --> 00:08:02,970
Nothing can come between us!

140
00:08:02,970 --> 00:08:04,750
S-Sure, but still...

141
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:07,280
Or let me guess.

142
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:10,540
Are you <i>actually</i> into me like that?

143
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:14,180
O-Of course not.

144
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,380
Stop, Yu!

145
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,050
I'm just jokin—

146
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:18,800
Morning, Hii-chan.

147
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,640
Oh hey, Enocchi.

148
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,480
Let's go, Yu-kun!

149
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:24,330
Y-Yeah.

150
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:29,290
Hii-chan, I can't wait for our sleepover!

151
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:35,000
<i>What's on my mind, you ask?</i>

152
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:38,430
<i>Yu's been too busy paying attention 
to Enocchi recently.</i>

153
00:08:39,910 --> 00:08:41,890
Yu-kun! Open wide!

154
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:43,900
Ahh...

155
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,000
I-I think that's enough.

156
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:51,090
I found somewhere away from others 
so you wouldn't get embarrassed.

157
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,940
Yeah, but still...

158
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:56,200
It's embarrassing enough 
without anyone watching.

159
00:08:56,510 --> 00:08:58,970
I wouldn't complain too much, if I were you.

160
00:08:58,970 --> 00:09:00,050
<i>Enomoto-san, help!</i>

161
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:04,480
Enomoto-san, HELP

162
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:04,480
Himari was waiting for me!

163
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:01,240
<i>Himari was waiting for me.</i>

164
00:09:00,850 --> 00:09:04,480
Please! Please text back.

165
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,040
<i>Please! Please text back.</i>

166
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:04,480
Himari's talking about a sleepover.

167
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:04,480
I can't do this anymore, she's too cute.

168
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,480
<i>Himari's talking about a sleepover.</i>

169
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,480
<i>I can't do this anymore, she's too cute.</i>

170
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,480
I'm gonna lose my best friend.

171
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,480
Don't leave me on read

172
00:09:02,350 --> 00:09:04,480
I'll do anything!

173
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:04,480
Please help

174
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:08,440
<i>I feel violated.</i>

175
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:12,390
That drink isn't allowed when it's just us.

176
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:16,720
It's rude to bring 
in reminders of another girl.

177
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,260
Here.

178
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:20,380
Don't say it like that.

179
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:23,290
She's my rival at this point!

180
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:27,920
If you find her too cute to be her friend, 
just tell her how you feel.

181
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:32,240
Yu-kun, do you even <i>want</i> to date Hii-chan?

182
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,480
I dunno.

183
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:40,590
I like Himari, but opening 
my store comes before love.

184
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:45,920
Yup, you tend to make 
things difficult like that.

185
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,100
But I admire that.

186
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:53,200
It means you want both love and your dream.

187
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:58,120
You're so honest with yourself, 
and I love that about you.

188
00:09:59,190 --> 00:10:01,560
Take your sweet time with Hii-chan.

189
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,410
That way, I still have a chance to catch up!

190
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,970
I wish I had that mental fortitude.

191
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,920
<i>Everyone's busy practicing 
for the tournament.</i>

192
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,210
Yu!

193
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:17,010
Let's go shopping when 
you're done watering flowers!

194
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,700
<i>Himari's soft, supple skin!</i>

195
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,970
<i>Calm down, this is nothing new!</i>

196
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:24,680
Shopping? What for?

197
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:28,190
Yup! I want a swimsuit for summer break!

198
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:30,640
S-Swimsuit? Are you crazy?!

199
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:34,360
Asking a guy you're not even dating 
to help you pick out a swim—

200
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:36,100
<i>Hang on.</i>

201
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:38,200
<i>I did that last year.</i>

202
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:41,040
<i>What was I even thinking back then?</i>

203
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:44,180
Then let's invite Enomoto-san.

204
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:45,440
Why Enocchi?

205
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,380
Never mind, that's fine.

206
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:49,750
You'd probably invite her anyways.

207
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:51,750
Th-Then I'll go find her!

208
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,070
Hey, Enomoto-san.

209
00:10:59,210 --> 00:11:01,600
<i>Himari's arch nemesis, Iron Claw!</i>

210
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,310
Ouch...

211
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:07,460
"Himari wants to shop for swimsuits. 
Help, Enomoto-san!"

212
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:12,480
You're not inviting me to see
 <i>me</i> in a swimsuit, are you?

213
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,100
I-I'm sorry!

214
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:19,670
This seemed like a "Bwa-ha!" situation, 
so I recruited your support.

215
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:21,360
Don't go then.

216
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:24,570
B-But she's my best friend.

217
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,380
<i>"All that genuine talk for what?"</i>

218
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:30,440
<i>"You're like any other guy."</i>

219
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,290
<i>I wanna see Himari in a swimsuit. Sue me.</i>

220
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:38,590
I have band practice today, 
so you'll have to survive on your own.

221
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:40,250
O-Okay.

222
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,860
That's cute!

223
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:44,230
You're way too close!

224
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,220
Yu, what do you think?

225
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,190
I-I should go hom—

226
00:11:47,190 --> 00:11:48,790
Come on!

227
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:50,330
You're choking me!

228
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:52,250
Pick something out yourself!

229
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:54,880
You're not one to care what others think.

230
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:56,720
Yeah, but...

231
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,770
I'm getting this to show you.

232
00:11:58,770 --> 00:12:00,520
I wanna get something you'll like.

233
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,110
O-Oh.

234
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:05,260
What's this, Yu-kun?

235
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:07,470
Are you blushing, by chance?

236
00:12:07,470 --> 00:12:08,430
Sh-Shut up.

237
00:12:08,430 --> 00:12:10,540
Stop teasing me like that.

238
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,540
Bwa-ha!

239
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:14,040
I swear, you'll fall for that forever.

240
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,330
Let's go inside!

241
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:20,290
Y-Yeah, let's start over there.

242
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,060
<i>The innocent dress type?</i>

243
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:27,430
<i>Or the vibrant two-piece?</i>

244
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:30,350
Look at all these florals!

245
00:12:30,350 --> 00:12:31,310
Which one do you like?

246
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:32,730
<i>Touché, Himari!</i>

247
00:12:32,730 --> 00:12:36,400
<i>She knows I like cute designs 
more than raunchy ones!</i>

248
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,780
Th-They all look fine.

249
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:40,640
Then lemme try them on!

250
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,610
<i>I feel so uncomfortable...</i>

251
00:12:44,610 --> 00:12:45,920
Yu!

252
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:47,330
Y-You done?

253
00:12:47,990 --> 00:12:49,490
Guess what?

254
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:54,450
I actually have a super 
raunchy piece on right now.

255
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,570
You weren't looking at anything like that!

256
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,000
Oh, but I was!

257
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
With tiny straps.

258
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:04,910
Y-You liar!

259
00:13:04,910 --> 00:13:07,000
They don't even sell those designs out here!

260
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:10,010
You sure about that?

261
00:13:10,010 --> 00:13:12,690
<i>Th-This is where she usually goes, "Bwa-ha!"</i>

262
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:16,640
<i>But what if she's telling 
the truth? I'd die!</i>

263
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:22,940
S-Sorry, gotta go!

264
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:28,640
<i>I chickened out.</i>

265
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:32,240
<i>How can she pull that shit in public?</i>

266
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:34,670
Hey, idiot.

267
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,820
You have a guest.

268
00:13:42,190 --> 00:13:43,480
Nice to meet you.

269
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,880
I'm Kureha Enomoto.

270
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:50,940
Shinji-kun's told me all about you, Yu-chan.

271
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:53,120
I've heard you're good friends with Rion.

272
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:56,060
Kureha-san, you know Makishima?

273
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:58,190
Yup, we're old neighbors.

274
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,510
Oh...

275
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:00,570
So, Kureha.

276
00:14:01,330 --> 00:14:02,980
What's your visit about?

277
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:05,920
Right, I totally forgot.

278
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:09,790
Can I have your Himari-chan? Pretty please?

279
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:17,630
Scumbag womanizer. Come here.

280
00:14:19,090 --> 00:14:23,020
Hey. Yu's been acting weird lately.

281
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:25,300
You got in his head again, didn't you?

282
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:26,770
Natsu? Acting weird?

283
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:29,360
He's been avoiding me like the plague.

284
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:32,720
And he always makes sure Enocchi tags along.

285
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:36,170
Well isn't it obvious?

286
00:14:36,170 --> 00:14:38,400
Natsu's finally fed up with you.

287
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,350
He's switched over to Rin-chan.

288
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:44,610
Would you bet your racket on that?

289
00:14:43,970 --> 00:14:44,610
Wait.

290
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:47,310
No roughhousing with the racket.

291
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,500
Ugh, that's totally unfair.

292
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,080
Give me my racket.

293
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,750
To tell you the truth, 
I haven't done anything.

294
00:15:00,950 --> 00:15:03,500
Or rather, I have no reason to do anything.

295
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:06,470
Luckily, Kureha-san took care of that.

296
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:10,090
<i>The chocolate cosmos represents...</i>

297
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:11,770
<i>"The end of love."</i>

298
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:14,880
I'm sure you've heard about this,

299
00:15:15,110 --> 00:15:19,160
but Himari-chan was 
supposed to join our agency.

300
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:21,160
She made it sound like she was coming,

301
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,780
then suddenly quit out of nowhere.

302
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,520
I-I'm sorry to cause you trouble.

303
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:31,020
It's okay. I'm not mad.

304
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:34,420
I only came up with the idea 
and convinced the CEO.

305
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:38,240
And funded all expenses out of pocket.

306
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:41,740
All to get kicked 
to the curb by Himari-chan.

307
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:43,680
Why would I be mad?

308
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:48,080
I came to talk business with you, Yu-chan.

309
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,130
Business?

310
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:54,100
Can you talk to Himari-chan 
so she joins our agency?

311
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:56,300
But Himari and I have—

312
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,360
I've heard.

313
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:59,850
You have a dream to open your own store.

314
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:02,560
But this is the middle of nowhere.

315
00:16:02,730 --> 00:16:04,560
Don't you think that's a bit unrealistic?

316
00:16:05,870 --> 00:16:07,850
I'm not asking you to give that up for free.

317
00:16:08,930 --> 00:16:10,320
What's that for?

318
00:16:10,510 --> 00:16:12,150
Duh, silly!

319
00:16:12,150 --> 00:16:13,960
It's in exchange for Himari-chan.

320
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:18,340
I'll pay you cash in advance 
for her future earnings.

321
00:16:20,530 --> 00:16:23,020
Oh right! And models, too.

322
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,880
You'll need a girl to take her place.

323
00:16:26,330 --> 00:16:29,430
Feel free to pick anyone 
you like from our agency.

324
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:31,280
I've heard enough!

325
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,680
Himari isn't a thing you can buy!

326
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:36,720
No money or model will change my mind!

327
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,990
It's my dream to open 
a store together with Himari.

328
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:42,880
If I can't do it with her, 
none of it matters!

329
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,040
Oh, I get it.

330
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,560
She's super important to you.

331
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:52,640
I totally get why. She's so cute!

332
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:56,060
Honestly, it's pure talent.

333
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,240
But isn't it a shame?

334
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:03,320
She's basically squashing 
that for someone else's mediocre talent.

335
00:17:04,050 --> 00:17:07,920
Are you saying 
I'm squashing Himari's talent?

336
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:09,500
Yup!

337
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:17,410
Honestly, even in middle school, 
your pieces were pretty amateur.

338
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:21,430
And your work now 
is hardly more than ordinary.

339
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:28,740
You're crushing your best friend's 
talent for selfish reasons.

340
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:31,750
Would you call that true friendship?

341
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:32,740
Oh, wait!

342
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:35,450
You're not business partners.

343
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:39,650
You just can't let Himari-chan go 
because you like her.

344
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:41,170
Th-That's not true.

345
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:42,440
So what's your choice?

346
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:46,440
If you can devote your life to loving her,

347
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:48,920
I'll let you come to Tokyo with us.

348
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,880
But you'll have to give up your dream.

349
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:58,990
<i>I don't think she's right.</i>

350
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:03,430
<i>But... could this be Himari's big break?</i>

351
00:18:03,430 --> 00:18:06,290
See, you can't commit either way.

352
00:18:06,730 --> 00:18:09,420
You two just wanna have fun.

353
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:13,110
Neither of you are serious 
about your dreams.

354
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:14,220
Stop right there!

355
00:18:14,550 --> 00:18:17,610
I won't let you lay a finger on Yu-kun!

356
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,080
Hibari-kun.

357
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:22,280
Oops, I forgot to lock the door.

358
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:24,160
Hibari-san, how did you know?

359
00:18:24,470 --> 00:18:26,960
Himari called, so I rushed over.

360
00:18:28,450 --> 00:18:33,170
Kureha-kun, I see you've been toying 
with my dear Yu-kun.

361
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:38,130
I would never! I was just talking business.

362
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:43,180
Business would involve merit 
for both parties.

363
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:44,850
I see you haven't changed one bit.

364
00:18:44,850 --> 00:18:47,170
Saku-nee-san, are those two...

365
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:50,360
True business is about 
achieving mutual benefits.

366
00:18:47,170 --> 00:18:50,360
Can't you tell? They're exes.

367
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:56,120
I won't allow Himari and Yu-kun's 
friendship to suffer a single blow.

368
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:01,060
There's that tough guy front again.

369
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:01,720
Here.

370
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:06,920
Hibari-san?!

371
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:12,910
Stay out of it unless you want this 
video plastered all over the internet.

372
00:19:12,910 --> 00:19:15,040
Please, don't! Kureha-kun!

373
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:16,880
That has nothing to do with this!

374
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:19,640
<i>You</i> have nothing to do with this.

375
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:27,510
Remember how you swore off real women?

376
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:30,350
You can't touch my phone 
as long as it's tucked in here.

377
00:19:30,350 --> 00:19:31,800
Why you—!

378
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:34,390
Then... take this!

379
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:38,120
So scary!

380
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:40,280
Sakura-chan, here!

381
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,280
Don't drag me into this.

382
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,240
You can't blackmail me anymo—

383
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:52,040
I have twenty backups 
for work, just in case!

384
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,960
You tricked me!

385
00:19:54,510 --> 00:19:57,030
I've never seen this side of Hibari-san...

386
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:59,270
He's always been like this.

387
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:02,590
Why don't you two get back together already?

388
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:04,000
No way!

389
00:20:04,470 --> 00:20:09,320
We're getting nowhere 
with you two doing the talking.

390
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,530
Kureha, you may think 
you're doing the right thing,

391
00:20:12,530 --> 00:20:15,290
but you can't push your ideals onto others.

392
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:21,080
I get why you see yourself in Himari-chan.

393
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:26,910
But you hated being told what 
to do more than anyone.

394
00:20:27,390 --> 00:20:30,500
I knew I shouldn't have 
asked Sakura-chan for help.

395
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:33,860
You're always the voice of reason.

396
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,070
I've changed my mind!

397
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,430
Yu-chan, let's go head to head.

398
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:39,790
Head to head?

399
00:20:39,790 --> 00:20:44,540
Take the summer to make 
your best masterpiece.

400
00:20:44,990 --> 00:20:47,510
Prove me wrong with 
the quality of your work.

401
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:53,740
You should be thanking me 
for even considering this option.

402
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:54,920
What do you mean?

403
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:58,480
Like I said, I've been paying 
for Himari-chan out of pocket.

404
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:02,980
I don't know any high schooler 
who'd be able to pay this off.

405
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:07,180
Kureha, you mean 
if my idiot brother said no,

406
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:09,710
you were planning to blackmail 
Himari-chan with debt?

407
00:21:09,950 --> 00:21:12,380
You're so smart, Sakura-chan! Yup!

408
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:17,230
The only person who can help Himari-chan 
is her best friend Yu-chan.

409
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:18,290
Are you in?

410
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:31,180
If I win, will you wipe her slate clean?

411
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,820
Sure!

412
00:21:32,820 --> 00:21:35,850
If I lose, I'll give up 
Himari-chan and the money.

413
00:21:36,210 --> 00:21:40,120
But if I win, hand her over to me.

414
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:42,400
Alright.

415
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:45,360
The theme is "memories of summer."

416
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,530
You have until the Obon festival in August.

417
00:21:48,530 --> 00:21:50,010
I'll be back then!

418
00:21:55,350 --> 00:21:59,720
<i>Are my accessories really 
worth Himari's devotion?</i>

419
00:22:00,930 --> 00:22:04,360
<i>It was time to put that to the test.</i>

420
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:39,890
The Meaning Behind Sunflowers

